Confirmed the two backend checkouts are in sync (only `.env` differs, which is expected/local). I now have all the ground truth needed. Here is the concrete implementation plan.

---

# Motoboy → Real Supabase Auth Migration Plan

## 0. Naming of new pieces (referenced throughout)

- New backend endpoint (JwtGuard-protected, "complete motoboy profile after client-side signUp"): `POST /motoboy/onboarding/completar-cadastro` in a new `motoboy-onboarding.controller.ts`, backed by a renamed/refactored `MotoboyAuthService` (keep the class name, gut its contents).
- New "claim session" endpoint: `POST /motoboy/auth/abrir-sessao` (JwtGuard-protected, Bearer = real Supabase token).
- New guard: `MotoboyGuard` rewritten in place (same file/class name `src/auth/motoboy.guard.ts`, `MotoboyGuard`) — composes `JwtGuard` + `motoboys` lookup by `user_id` + `x-motoboy-session` check, mirroring `RestaurantOwnerGuard`'s composition pattern.
- New custom header: `x-motoboy-session: <sessionId>` (replaces `x-motoboy-token`).
- New frontend `sessionId` storage key: `motoboy_session_id` (localStorage), sitting alongside the Supabase SDK's own session (which already persists via `src/lib/supabase.js`, `persistSession:true`).

## 1. SQL migrations (`deliveryhub_white_label/supabase/migrations/`)

One migration file, e.g. `20260821000001_motoboys_supabase_auth.sql`:

- No structural change needed to `motoboys.user_id` — it already exists (`20260714000002_motoboys_user_id.sql`), nullable, `REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL`. Leave as-is.
- **Do not drop** `password_hash`, `access_token`, `active_session_id`, `session_expires_at`, `precisa_completar_cadastro` — keep for audit/rollback safety per project convention, but stop reading/writing `password_hash`/`access_token` in new code paths (see §2). Add a `COMMENT ON COLUMN public.motoboys.password_hash IS 'Legado — cadastros migrados pra Supabase Auth. Não usado em novos fluxos.'` (and similarly for `access_token`) so the deprecation is discoverable in `\d motoboys`, matching the existing style of comments on `criado_por_restaurant_id`/`restaurant_id`.
- Add a **partial unique index enforcing `user_id` uniqueness** if not already implied: check first — `user_id UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id)` has no UNIQUE today, meaning nothing stops two `motoboys` rows pointing at the same `auth.users.id`. Add `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS motoboys_user_id_unique ON public.motoboys (user_id) WHERE user_id IS NOT NULL;` — this is a correctness gap the new flow depends on (the new guard does `.eq('user_id', userId).maybeSingle()`; without uniqueness a bad insert could silently create two motoboy rows for one identity and break that lookup or return the wrong row).
- **`motoboys.email`**: leave the existing partial unique index (`WHERE email IS NOT NULL`) alone; do not make it `NOT NULL` at the DB level (some very old rows plausibly have phone-only). Enforce "email mandatory for new/updated accounts" purely in application code (both `criarPeloRestaurante` and the new onboarding endpoint), consistent with how `precisa_completar_cadastro` etc. were application-enforced historically.
- **RLS `motoboys_owner` policy** (keys off legacy `restaurant_id`, not `criado_por_restaurant_id`): flag as **out of scope** for this migration. Verified: `SupabaseService` (`src/supabase/supabase.service.ts`) always uses `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, which bypasses RLS entirely, and no frontend code queries `public.motoboys` with the anon key (`Grep` for `from('motoboys')` in `deliveryhub_white_label/src` returns nothing) — so this policy is already dead code with zero behavioral effect. Worth a follow-up cleanup ticket, not blocking this migration. Mention this explicitly in the migration file as a comment so a future reader doesn't assume it's load-bearing.
- No change needed to the `user_role` enum (`'motoboy'` already present) or to `handle_new_user()` (already promotes `role` from `raw_user_meta_data->>'role'`, which the new self-signup will set to `'motoboy'` directly — no more relying on the optional post-hoc `vincularContaCliente()` promotion path).

Local apply: `npx supabase migration up` from `deliveryhub_white_label/`. Production: `npx supabase db push --linked` **only after explicit user confirmation**, and only after the backfill script (§3) has been run against local/staging and reviewed — never automatically.

## 2. Backend changes (apply identically to both `serer_delivery` and `server_delivery` submodule)

### 2.1 `src/motoboy/motoboy-auth.service.ts` — gutted and repurposed

Remove: `login()`, `completarCadastro()`, `gerarToken()`, the `bcrypt`/`jsonwebtoken` imports, `CadastroMotoboyBody.password`/`supabase_access_token` handling for a not-yet-authenticated caller, `exigirContaSemRestaurante`/`vincularContaCliente` (superseded — see below).

Keep/repurpose:
- `EMAIL_RE`, `PHONE_RE` (still exported, still used by `motoboy.service.ts` for `criarPeloRestaurante`/`editarPeloRestaurante` validation).
- `uploadDocumento()` (unchanged — still uploads to private `motoboy-documentos` bucket).
- The single-session logic (`abrirSessao`, `SESSION_TTL_MS`, `logout`) — moves conceptually to be keyed by `motoboyId` looked up via `user_id`, not a custom JWT payload. Keep the atomic conditional-`UPDATE ... OR (active_session_id IS NULL OR session_expires_at < now())` exactly as-is; it's storage-agnostic to how the caller was authenticated.

New methods on `MotoboyAuthService`:
- `async completarCadastro(userId: string, body: CompletarCadastroMotoboyBody)` — the self-signup replacement. Body: `{ name, phone, foto_perfil, documento_frente, documento_verso?, comprovante_endereco }` (no `password`, no `email` — email now comes from the verified Supabase JWT via `SupabaseJwtService`/`JwtGuard`, not client input, so it can't be spoofed). Logic, modeled directly on `OnboardingController.registrarInicial`'s idempotency pattern:
  1. Reject if this `userId` already has a `restaurants` row (mirrors today's `exigirContaSemRestaurante`, now unconditional since we always have a real `userId`).
  2. Reject if this `userId` already has a `motoboys` row (idempotency guard — reload-safe, matches `registrarInicial`'s `existing` check).
  3. Pull `email` from the JWT (`req.userRole`/verified payload `email` claim — Supabase JWTs include `email`) rather than trusting client body.
  4. Insert `motoboys` row with `user_id: userId`, `email`, `name`, `phone`, `precisa_completar_cadastro: false`, `status_plataforma: 'pendente'` (unchanged behavior — still needs platform approval), **no `password_hash`**.
  5. Upload the 4 documents exactly as today.
  6. Promote `user_profiles.role = 'motoboy'` for this `userId` (this replaces `vincularContaCliente`'s promotion — now unconditional/mandatory, not "if a token happened to be passed").
  7. Return `{ ok: true }` — no token; the frontend already has its Supabase session from `signUp()`, then separately calls the claim-session endpoint (§2.2) to get `sessionId`.
- `async abrirSessaoPortal(userId: string): Promise<{ sessionId: string }>` — the decision-#1 "claim session" logic: look up `motoboys.id` by `user_id = userId` (404 `NotFoundException` if none — not a motoboy account), check `is_active` (403 if disabled), then call the existing `abrirSessao(motoboyId)` (unchanged atomic claim), return `{ sessionId }`.
- Keep `logout(motoboyId)` but change its call site to resolve `motoboyId` from `req.userId` via the new guard (no longer takes a raw `motoboyId` from a JWT payload).

`CadastroMotoboyBody` interface: rename to `CompletarCadastroMotoboyBody`, drop `password`/`email`/`supabase_access_token` fields.

### 2.2 New controller: `src/motoboy/motoboy-auth.controller.ts` (keep file, rewrite contents)

```
@Controller('motoboy/auth')
export class MotoboyAuthController {
  @Post('completar-cadastro')
  @UseGuards(JwtGuard)
  completarCadastro(@Body() body, @Req() req) { return service.completarCadastro(req.userId, body); }

  @Post('abrir-sessao')
  @UseGuards(JwtGuard)
  @Throttle(...)  // keep some rate limit, e.g. same 5/min as old login
  abrirSessao(@Req() req) { return service.abrirSessaoPortal(req.userId); }

  @Post('logout')
  @UseGuards(MotoboyGuard)   // new guard, needs both Bearer + x-motoboy-session
  logout(@Req() req) { return service.logout(req.motoboyId); }
}
```
Remove the old `POST cadastro` and `POST login` routes entirely (no more email/phone+password custom login — Supabase Auth handles that client-side via `supabase.auth.signInWithPassword`). Keep `@Throttle` decorators on `completar-cadastro` (still public-ish, still creates a DB row + uploads files) and `abrir-sessao` (still a sensitive session-claiming operation, keep a rate limit like 10/min to blunt session-lock abuse).

### 2.3 `src/auth/motoboy.guard.ts` — rewritten, same class/file

```ts
@Injectable()
export class MotoboyGuard implements CanActivate {
  constructor(private jwtGuard: JwtGuard, private supabase: SupabaseService) {}

  async canActivate(context): Promise<boolean> {
    await this.jwtGuard.canActivate(context);   // sets req.userId, req.userRole
    const request = context.switchToHttp().getRequest();
    const sessionHeader = request.headers['x-motoboy-session'] as string | undefined;
    if (!sessionHeader) throw new UnauthorizedException('Sessão de motoboy necessária');

    const { data } = await this.supabase.client
      .from('motoboys')
      .select('id, name, is_active, active_session_id, session_expires_at')
      .eq('user_id', request.userId)
      .maybeSingle();

    if (!data) throw new UnauthorizedException('Conta não é de um motoboy');
    if (!data.is_active) throw new ForbiddenException('Conta desativada');

    const sessaoValida =
      data.active_session_id === sessionHeader &&
      !!data.session_expires_at &&
      new Date(data.session_expires_at).getTime() > Date.now();
    if (!sessaoValida) throw new UnauthorizedException('Sessão encerrada. Faça login novamente.');

    request.motoboyId = data.id;
    request.motoboyName = data.name;
    return true;
  }
}
```
This is exactly the `RestaurantOwnerGuard` composition pattern (run `JwtGuard.canActivate` first, then a DB lookup keyed by `req.userId`) plus the extra session-header check decision #1 requires. Drop `MotoboyJwtPayload`, the `jsonwebtoken`/`MOTOBOY_JWT_SECRET` usage, and the legacy `access_token` fallback branch entirely (no more `precisa_completar_cadastro` pre-password link flow — dead once cutover completes; see §5 on when it's safe to actually delete vs. leave inert).

`src/auth/auth.module.ts`: `MotoboyGuard` now depends on `JwtGuard` (already a provider in the same module) — no module wiring change needed beyond the constructor injection, since `AuthModule` already provides both.

